<%- include('partials/head') %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>

<main id="main">

  <%- include('partials/page-hero', {
    eyebrow: 'Legal',
    eyebrowIcon: 'shield',
    heroTitle: 'Privacy Policy',
    heroIntro: 'How Zenvorali Cleaning collects, uses, stores, shares and protects personal information belonging to our clients, website visitors, job applicants and suppliers in Kansas City, Missouri and across the metro.',
    heroPoints: null,
    breadcrumbs: [{ name: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy-policy' }]
  }) %>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose prose--legal reveal">
        <p class="legal-meta"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 4 October 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Effective:</strong> 4 October 2026</p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how <strong><%= site.legalName %></strong> ("Zenvorali Cleaning",
          "we", "us" or "our") handles personal information. We are a cleaning services company located
          at <%= site.address.full %>, and we provide residential and commercial cleaning services across
          the Kansas City metropolitan area in Missouri and Kansas.
        </p>
        <p>
          We have written this policy in plain English rather than legal boilerplate, because a privacy
          policy is only useful if the person reading it can actually understand what they are agreeing to.
          If anything here is unclear, contact us at <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a>
          and we will explain it.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>We collect the following categories of personal information:</p>
        <h3>1.1 Information you give us directly</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact details</strong> — your name, phone number, email address and service address, provided when you request a quote or book a service.</li>
          <li><strong>Property information</strong> — the size, layout, condition and access details of the property to be cleaned, including any pets present, alarm codes and entry instructions.</li>
          <li><strong>Service preferences</strong> — scheduling preferences, product sensitivities, allergies in the household and any instructions you ask us to record.</li>
          <li><strong>Payment information</strong> — billing details and payment method. We do not store full card numbers on our own systems; card payments are processed by our payment processor.</li>
          <li><strong>Correspondence</strong> — records of calls, emails, text messages and form submissions between you and our team.</li>
          <li><strong>Employment applications</strong> — if you apply for a role: your CV, work history, references, identity documents and the results of background checks and drug screening, where lawful and with your consent.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>1.2 Information collected automatically when you use our website</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Technical data</strong> — IP address, browser type and version, device type, operating system, screen size and referring URL.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage data</strong> — pages viewed, time on page, links clicked and search terms entered within our site.</li>
          <li><strong>Cookie data</strong> — as described in section 7 below.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>1.3 Information from third parties</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Referrals</strong> — where a client refers you to us, we receive your name and contact details from that client, with their confirmation that you are happy to be contacted.</li>
          <li><strong>Background check providers</strong> — for job applicants only, and only after you have been informed and consented.</li>
          <li><strong>Review platforms</strong> — where you leave a public review of our services.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We use personal information for the following purposes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Providing our services</strong> — scheduling visits, dispatching crews to the correct address, completing the agreed scope of work and recording what was done.</li>
          <li><strong>Quoting and invoicing</strong> — preparing flat-rate quotes, issuing invoices, processing payments and maintaining accounting records.</li>
          <li><strong>Communication</strong> — confirming appointments, sending arrival notifications, responding to enquiries and following up on completed work.</li>
          <li><strong>Service quality</strong> — inspecting completed jobs, handling guarantee claims and improving our checklists and training.</li>
          <li><strong>Safety and security</strong> — maintaining key and alarm code records, verifying identity, protecting our staff and clients, and preventing fraud.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal compliance</strong> — meeting tax, insurance, employment and record-keeping obligations.</li>
          <li><strong>Marketing</strong> — sending offers, seasonal reminders and service updates, but only where you have opted in or where we have an existing client relationship and the message relates to similar services. You can opt out at any time.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
        <p>Where applicable law requires us to identify a legal basis for processing, we rely on the following:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contract</strong> — processing necessary to provide the cleaning services you have booked, including scheduling, access and invoicing.</li>
          <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — operating and improving our business, maintaining service quality, preventing fraud and protecting our staff, where these interests are not overridden by your rights.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — retaining records where tax, employment or insurance law requires it.</li>
          <li><strong>Consent</strong> — for marketing communications where consent is required, and for background checks on job applicants. You may withdraw consent at any time.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. How We Share Information</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it with third parties for their own marketing purposes.</strong>
          We share information only in the following limited circumstances:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Our employees and crew members</strong> — the cleaners assigned to your property receive the address, access details and any relevant instructions. They do not receive payment information.</li>
          <li><strong>Payment processors</strong> — to charge your card or process an ACH transfer.</li>
          <li><strong>Insurance providers</strong> — where necessary to process a damage or liability claim.</li>
          <li><strong>Professional advisers</strong> — accountants, auditors and legal advisers, bound by confidentiality obligations.</li>
          <li><strong>Background check providers</strong> — for job applicants, with consent.</li>
          <li><strong>Building management offices</strong> — for clients in managed buildings, we may provide our company name and insurance certificate to register for access. We do not disclose your personal contact details.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal authorities</strong> — where we are required by law, court order or valid legal process to disclose information.</li>
          <li><strong>Business transfer</strong> — if our business is sold or merged, client records may transfer to the successor entity, which would remain bound by this policy.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. How Long We Keep Information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Client service records</strong> — retained for seven years after your last service, to satisfy tax and accounting requirements and to honour guarantee claims.</li>
          <li><strong>Access information</strong> — key and alarm codes are deleted within 30 days of your final service or on request, whichever is sooner.</li>
          <li><strong>Marketing preferences</strong> — retained until you opt out, after which we keep a minimal record that you have opted out so we do not contact you again.</li>
          <li><strong>Job applications</strong> — retained for 12 months for unsuccessful applicants unless you ask us to keep them longer.</li>
          <li><strong>Website analytics</strong> — aggregated and retained for a maximum of 26 months.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. How We Protect Information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Access to client records is limited to staff who need it to perform their role.</li>
          <li>Keys and alarm codes are stored in a locked key cabinet with logged in-and-out sign-out procedures; codes are stored in an access-controlled system.</li>
          <li>Electronic records are protected by password authentication, encryption in transit and access logging.</li>
          <li>Employees receive confidentiality training and sign confidentiality agreements as a condition of employment.</li>
          <li>Background checks and identity verification are completed for every employee before they access client information.</li>
          <li>Paper records containing personal information are stored securely and shredded when no longer required.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          No security system is perfect. If we become aware of a breach that is likely to result in a risk
          to your rights, we will notify affected individuals and any relevant authorities without undue
          delay, as required by applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Cookies and Website Analytics</h2>
        <p>Our website uses a small number of cookies and similar technologies:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Strictly necessary cookies</strong> — required for the site to function, including security and session handling. These cannot be disabled.</li>
          <li><strong>Preference cookies</strong> — remember choices you make, such as form entries, so you do not have to re-enter them.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics cookies</strong> — help us understand which pages are useful and how visitors navigate the site. Data is aggregated and not used to identify individuals.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings. Disabling analytics cookies does
          not affect your ability to use the site or to book a service.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>Subject to applicable law and to certain exemptions, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal information we hold about you.</li>
          <li><strong>Correct</strong> information that is inaccurate or incomplete.</li>
          <li><strong>Delete</strong> information we no longer need, subject to our legal retention obligations.</li>
          <li><strong>Restrict or object</strong> to certain processing, including direct marketing.</li>
          <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive a copy of information you provided to us in a structured, commonly used format.</li>
          <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time where processing is based on consent.</li>
          <li><strong>Non-discrimination</strong> — we will not refuse service or charge different prices because you exercised a privacy right.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a>
          or call <a href="<%= site.phoneHref %>"><%= site.phone %></a>. We will respond within 45 days and
          will confirm your identity before acting on a request to protect your information.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our services are directed at adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
          children under 16. Our cleaners will of course be present in homes where children live, but we do
          not create records about those children beyond a general note where relevant to safe cleaning
          practice, such as avoiding certain products around an infant.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Do Not Track Signals</h2>
        <p>
          Some browsers transmit "Do Not Track" signals. There is not yet a common industry standard for
          interpreting these, so our site does not currently respond to them. We do honour opt-out
          preferences for marketing and analytics where you have communicated them to us.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy to reflect changes in our practices or legal requirements. When we make
          material changes, we will update the "Last updated" date at the top and, where the change is
          significant, notify active clients by email. We encourage you to review this page periodically.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>If you have questions, concerns or complaints about how we handle your information:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a></li>
          <li><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="<%= site.phoneHref %>"><%= site.phone %></a></li>
          <li><strong>Post:</strong> <%= site.legalName %>, <%= site.address.line1 %>, <%= site.address.city %>, <%= site.address.state %> <%= site.address.zip %></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you are not satisfied with our response, you may escalate your concern to the relevant state
          attorney general's office or consumer protection authority in Missouri or Kansas.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ POLICY NOTES ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2 class="section__title">How We Handle Your Information in Practice</h2>
        <p>
          A privacy policy is easier to trust when it is explained rather than merely served. These are the
          practical answers to what actually happens to the information you give us, written in plain
          language alongside the formal terms above.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What we collect and why.</strong> We ask for your name, phone number, email address and
          property address because we cannot quote or dispatch a crew without them. If you give us access
          instructions, alarm codes or lockbox details, those are stored with your account and shared only
          with the crew assigned to your property.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What we do not do.</strong> We do not sell your details, rent them to marketing lists, or
          share them with third parties for advertising. We do not record photographs of the inside of your
          property for marketing use without asking you in writing first, and you are free to say no.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>How long we keep it.</strong> Booking and invoice records are retained as long as tax and
          accounting rules require. Access codes and alarm details are removed from your account as soon as
          you tell us they are no longer needed, or when your service ends.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Marketing contact.</strong> If you receive a reminder or an occasional offer from us by
          email or text, you can opt out with a single reply and we will action it manually rather than
          routing you through a preference centre. Transactional messages about a booking you have made are
          separate and will continue while a job is active.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Requesting your data.</strong> Email <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a>
          and we will tell you what we hold about you and delete anything we are not obliged to retain. We
          answer these requests directly rather than through a portal, and we do not charge for them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/cta', {
    ctaEyebrow: 'Questions about your data?',
    ctaTitle: 'We Are Happy to Explain Anything Here',
    ctaText: 'If any part of this policy is unclear, call us and a real person will walk you through it without the legal language.'
  }) %>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
<button class="to-top" id="toTop" type="button" aria-label="Back to top"><%- icon('chevronDown', 22) %></button>
